---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
import { portfolio } from '../data/site';
---

<Layout>
  <section class="container company-hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">OUR STORY / AN IMAGINED COMPANY, A CONSIDERED IDEA</p>
    <h1>
      A little less friction.
      <br />
      <em>A lot more possibility.</em>
    </h1>
    <p class="intro-copy">
      CIVOLYN began as a question: what would business software feel like if it
      made more room for the people using it?
    </p>
  </section>
  <figure class="container">
    <div class="company-landscape">
      <img
        src="/images/clarity-architecture-1440.webp"
        srcset="/images/clarity-architecture-640.webp 640w, /images/clarity-architecture-960.webp 960w, /images/clarity-architecture-1440.webp 1440w"
        sizes="(max-width: 1440px) 92vw, 1320px"
        width="1440"
        height="960"
        alt="An open cobalt arch in warm limestone architecture, an original visual study of space and clarity."
        fetchpriority="high"
      />
      <figcaption class="image-caption">
        Make room. An original architectural study for CIVOLYN.
      </figcaption>
    </div>
  </figure>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container story-section">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">WHY THIS IDEA EXISTS</p>
        <h2>
          More tools.
          <br />
          <em>Less clarity?</em>
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div class="editorial-copy">
        <p>
          A team can be well equipped and still spend its day looking for the
          next piece of context.
        </p>
        <p>
          The brief is in a document. The approval is in a message. The project
          status is in a spreadsheet someone updated yesterday. Each tool makes
          sense on its own. The work between them is where the friction lives.
        </p>
        <p>
          CIVOLYN is an imagined response to that familiar problem. It brings
          automation, shared knowledge and operational insight into a single
          product story. The aim is not to make every task automatic. It is to
          help people understand the work well enough to choose what happens
          next.
        </p>
        <p>
          There is no invented founding date, office or customer list behind
          this story. CIVOLYN is a fictional concept created for the ISMAIL
          portfolio, where the quality of the actual website is the work on
          show.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section feature-demo-section">
    <div class="container story-section">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">WHAT THE CONCEPT STANDS FOR</p>
        <h2>
          Good principles.
          <br />
          <em>Visible in the details.</em>
        </h2>
      </div>
      <ol class="values-list">
        <li>
          <span class="number">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Clarity is a feature.</h3>
            <p>
              A useful tool helps people understand what they are looking at.
              Clear labels, explicit states and readable explanations belong in
              the product from the start.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="number">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>People bring the judgment.</h3>
            <p>
              Context is rarely complete. Make room for questions, correction
              and a considered decision before work moves beyond the team.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="number">03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Connection should reduce effort.</h3>
            <p>
              Bringing tools together only matters if it makes the work easier
              to follow. A shared foundation should remove repetition, rather
              than create another layer to manage.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="number">04</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Details earn trust.</h3>
            <p>
              Say what is illustrative. Show where information comes from. Keep
              promises proportionate to what the interface actually does.
            </p>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container split-section">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">THE REAL WORK BEHIND THE FICTION</p>
        <h2>
          A product imagined.
          <br />
          <em>A website made real.</em>
        </h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>
          CIVOLYN demonstrates how visual identity, careful writing, responsive
          interfaces and considered interactions can work together to explain a
          complex offering.
        </p>
        <p>
          It is an original ISMAIL portfolio project, made for visitors who care
          how a business presents itself online. If that is the kind of
          attention your own website needs, the real conversation starts at
          ISMAIL.
        </p>
        <a class="arrow-link" href={portfolio}>
          Explore ISMAIL <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <CTA title="A more thoughtful way to explore what’s possible." />
</Layout>
